+# Guild exam and action feedback handoff
+
+## Regression report
+
+The server can have no commission while an `inventory_basic` promotion exam is
+already active. Previously each new decision retained only `/mycli guild status`;
+exam status and rejected starts were available solely through the full historical
+index. Live replies showed an active exam and `task_slot_busy`, followed by repeated
+promotion/start/status queries without a newly accepted physical task.
+
+The current-facts view now preserves the latest exact `/mycli guild exam status`
+reply independently of commission status. Catalogues cannot overwrite either.
+Each reply keeps its own observation time, age and historical label; login changes
+clear both caches. A complete tool response replaces earlier fragments for the same
+command, rather than mixing old and new status replies within two seconds.
+
+The latest explicitly non-read-only server attempt has a separate receipt pointer
+that subsequent queries do not replace. Its command, transport status and session
+remain visible; messages and structured records are exact field queries. All
+original command history and long feedback remain in immutable private evidence.
+`received` still does not establish gameplay success, and neither an index nor
+an empty commission report establishes that the exam is absent or completed.
+
+Before the fix, three regression cases failed. After the fix, the full Minecraft
+plugin suite passes 283 tests and Ruff passes for the changed Python files. Tests
+cover independent task scopes, catalogue interference, complete response replacement,
+out-of-order replies, login isolation, retained long feedback and exact readback.
+
+Only the Minecraft plugin needs reloading at an idle boundary. The native game,
+main brain, model, voice and observer can continue. Runtime acceptance must measure
+actual current-facts delivery, accepted tasks and outcomes separately: preparing
+this patch does not prove completion of the exam or sustained autonomous progress.
+
+## Local inference limits
+
+This change supports the user's complete-retention/current-facts/query policy. It
+does not truncate messages, add a periodic model call, reduce the retry interval,
+change model parameters, or reinstate generic history clipping. It also does not
+make an intentional whole-history query fit a 32K engine. Earlier capacity errors
+remain a separate issue; current successful requests and live gameplay must be
+measured rather than attributed to those older failures.
diff --git a/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/observations.py b/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/observations.py
